+
+Generic `join` and nonpair invitation acceptance start every open binding of the seat at the thread head. Undisplayed lazy messages addressed to the seat beyond its furthest cursor stay pending for the seat until the first top-level binding shows them; that pending mail settles once for the seat (subagents never see it). On a generic rejoin a binding skips joined-era mail another binding already read or passed (including by a fast-forward or a subagent's read), and lazy mail every binding had passed unshown is not offered again.
