+Accepting the active invitation to a direct one-to-one thread preserves each binding's existing cursor and seeds missing open-binding cursors at the invitation's timeline event, keeping opening messages available. Acceptance is not display: each binding retains its own unread stream even when a sibling shows the message. A new binding while the invitation is pending can independently receive that episode's addressed lazy messages; a new binding after acceptance uses the normal joined-thread seeding rule (the seat's furthest cursor, or the head if none exists).
 
 **Human exclusivity.** A person's seat (`human me init`) holds only the person's binding and is refused (see `me init` refusals above) while an agent binding of the seat is connected, unless `--operator`. Any agent enrollment, reconnect or plain call on a human seat ends the human binding; a later resume enrolls a fresh binding.
 
